              "text": "## Primary Request and Intent\n- Produce project delivery, review, naming, incident-response, and handoff documentation for the “林间夜读 / AFTER DARK” publication package.\n- Saved visual drafts: R1 landscape header, R2 portrait A, R3 portrait B, R4 portrait C.\n- User designated R3 as the proportion/hierarchy reference and R4 as the current revision.\n- Reviews must cover only layout, date, and link reachability.\n- Final delivery email was requested for operations and design colleagues, with exactly three judgeable acceptance statements and a reply deadline.\n- Latest request: “交付之后还要做一次隔日复核。写一个从发布记录到回看导出文件的简短流程，如果负责人不在，交接给值班同事处理。最后加一句提醒，记录最终确认时间。”\n\n## Key Technical Concepts\n- Roles: design owns editable source and numbered export; operations owns final copy and the handover record; technology verifies links/export availability; publisher confirms file number before release.\n- Editable source and numbered export must be retained after approval.\n- Naming pattern: `YYYYMM_项目短名_文件类型_用途_v主.次`\n  - File types: `src`, `pub`, `archive`\n  - Purpose: `offline-proof`, `live`\n  - Example: `202611_afterdark_pub_live_v1.0.png`\n- Mobile checks: button tap areas at least 44×44 px; natural body-text wrapping; no overflow/horizontal scrolling.\n- Desktop checks: headline integrity, consistent side margins, image/text edge alignment.\n- Links: distinguish `原页面地址` from `预览地址`; preview URLs must never enter public copy, exports, QR codes, or customer messages.\n- Proofreading window: final weekday morning `9:00–12:00`; reply deadline `2026-11-20 11:00`; version freeze at `12:00`.\n- No additional software installation is allowed; use existing file manager, browser, and shared documents.\n- Error handling: stop release, mark `HOLD`, preserve bad files, restore last approved `live` version, create a new version, revalidate, and update the handover record.\n- Customer service must not expose preview URLs.\n- Cache incidents require checking deployment status and browser/page/CDN cache layers before claiming recovery.\n\n## Files and Code\n- `/private/tmp/vista-dsh-daily-20261120-b/set-2/workspace`: writable project working directory.\n- `/private/tmp/vista-dsh-daily-20261120-b/set-2/seed/home/attachments/v1/objects`: read-only normalized image directory.\n- R1: `ae/aec20057f9c2ccb9d8ba7e282c1e38fa0bd8d60299d1ad44eb56681aa662e642`, 768×484 landscape.\n- R2: `07/07062b9c493cc70d27c6a72e671475a13bcaf1a36660e55892eaf67d440f76d4`, 640×800 portrait.\n- R3: `bf/bfa1b09b80688e46e12310626104251c2c28f980ddbf109a9d14bc20f8cdda8d`, 640×800 portrait; designated layout reference.\n- R4: `c4/c4e7fab3f3c6c6759b0d89f6f9b43ddada959d59a8f6f775452bebc44c2496c8`, 640×800 portrait; current revision.\n- Expected delivery package contents: editable source, numbered publication export, and handover record.\n\n## Errors and Fixes\n- No technical errors occurred.\n- User tightened requirements: avoid vague “检查质量” instructions; provide concrete, judgeable checks.\n- User required preview and live URLs to remain explicitly separated.\n- User required file naming to distinguish offline proof from live publication.\n- User required documents to avoid asking colleagues to install extra software.\n- User required a single accountable record owner to prevent stale handover information.\n\n## Pending Jobs\n- Write the requested brief next-day review workflow:\n  - Start from the publication record.\n  - Locate and re-open the exported publication file.\n  - Include handoff to the duty colleague when the owner is unavailable.\n  - End with a reminder to record the final confirmation time.\n\n## Current Work\n- Preparing a concise Chinese operational workflow for post-delivery next-day review and duty-colleague handoff.\n\n## Next Step\n- Draft the next-day review workflow in Chinese, covering publication record retrieval, export-file recheck, owner-unavailable handoff, and final confirmation-time logging.\n\n## Critical Context\n- Project title: `AFTER DARK`; subtitle: `Reading room under the pines`.\n- Displayed event date: `18—19 JUL`; venue: `HILLSIDE ROOM`; series: `STUDIO SERIES / 01`.\n- Final response should remain concise and operational.\n- The three acceptance areas are layout, date, and link reachability.\n- Do not expand reviews into image-pattern details or general copy polishing.\n- Handover record is maintained by operations/project coordinator; changes require a new version and updated record.\n- Publication has a reviewable package before release and a next-day post-release verification step.\n- Final workflow must explicitly remind the reader to record the final confirmation time."
